# Masks on a Micro level (a user report: masked eyes still moved). The mask brush paints the Micro level's own mask; Move and
# the Kelvin brushes move the base mesh below it. Move over a mask uses the grid's per-point rule; Kelvin Grab, started on a
# masked eye or dragged into it, does nothing near the mask (the cage held two rings out tore the surface), and works as ever
# away from it (it stops at the mask when dragged into it). tests/test_micro_mask_grab.cpp holds the geometry (every brush, bit-identical masked points).
run ui_look look=classic layout=classic
run new_sphere subdivisions=5
run micro_divide level=3
wait_idle 120
camera 0 0
key f
wait_idle 30
brush_size 45
hold ctrl
stroke 0.38 0.40 0.39 0.41 0.4
stroke 0.62 0.40 0.61 0.41 0.4
hold none
wait_idle 30

# Kelvin Grab pressed on an eye and dragged out: the base mesh doesn't move.
snapshot
click "KelvinGrab##brush.kelvingrab"
brush_size 140
stroke 0.38 0.40 0.30 0.28 0.6
wait_idle 30
expect_value moved == 0
key ctrl+z
wait_idle 30

# Away from the eyes (a small brush at the bottom of the sphere) Kelvin Grab moves the surface as ever.
snapshot
brush_size 40
stroke 0.50 0.75 0.56 0.80 0.6
wait_idle 30
expect_value moved > 0
